tags: guest-kernel, kernel

A setting of the start of the service: the guest kernel that the instance boots. It is
one setting for the instance and all its devices.

The value is the ids of the kernel image, one for each hash type, separated by commas
and sorted by their bytes. An id is <type>:<digest> in lowercase hexadecimal, where the
type is the digest of the empty input (REASON 6.3). The hash is of the bytes of the
kernel image file that the virtual machine loads. It is not the hash of an initial RAM
disk. Example, with one hash type: 0e57...a8:5c1f...9d.

With no setting, the service has no preference: the node selects the kernel. A node
boots a kernel only if the hash of its bytes, with the algorithm of one of the types,
is equal to the digest of that type. A node that does not have such a kernel refuses
the service. The node is bound.

The page size of the kernel must be one that the architecture of the container allows.
The node refuses a kernel with another page size: the software of the service can
depend on it.

=== formal
class=setting
default=absent: the node selects the kernel
hashed=the bytes of the kernel image file that the virtual machine loads, without an initial RAM disk
match=the node boots a kernel only if its hash with the algorithm of one type in the value is equal to the digest of that type
name=guest-kernel
page=the page size of the kernel is one that the architecture of the container allows; the node refuses a kernel with another page size
place=service.container.init
value=the ids <type>:<digest> of the kernel image, one for each hash type, lowercase hexadecimal, sorted, separated by commas
